10.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: No valid filtering strategy exists based solely on log2 fold change (or any thresholded DE metric) to remove cancer-gene contamination from one sample group. Log2FC is computed between your two biological conditions; any genes appearing as extreme DE due to unequal cancer-cell carryover after sorting are confounded with the true IL-15 effect you wish to measure. Applying an ad-hoc |log2FC| cutoff (e.g., via a one-liner such as `awk '$log2FoldChange > 5 {print $1}' results.tsv`) would therefore discard both contaminants and genuine biology, bias downstream enrichment tests, and is not statistically defensible. The correct approach requires an independent reference (e.g., RNA-seq of the pure cancer line) so that cancer-specific genes can be blacklisted by expression rank or by a decontamination algorithm (e.g., SoupX, DecontX) before DE testing; log2FC filtering alone cannot substitute for that information.

(The experimental design itself is also unbalanced—contamination confined to the CAR-only arm means any apparent IL-15 “rescue” signature is at least partly an artifact of differential purity.)

}

